n coming from our audience how  does that pad seven-hundred avoid the  facts of human error on the intermediate  precision as mentioned in IC h q - thank  you for that one so yeah a human error  particularly in calibration and system  suitability tests is arguably the  biggest problem so the p80 eliminates  manual data entry and manual  calculations which are arguably to be a  source of human error in the QC world  the calibration and system suitability  standard bottles carry an RFID tag which  allows the P 8,700 to recognize the  standards and upload and read their  certified value and check their use by  date so that eliminates the manual data  entry and then the P 8700 has automated  SOPs programmed in to allow it to carry  out the prescribed tests such as  calculator calibration and system  suitability and then calculate  automatically the pass/fail result so  there's no manual data transcription of  results that data is exported via  ethernet using password-protected PDF  files that secure File Transfer Protocol  so we completely remove the opportunity  for human error thank you very much Tony  and would you like to go ahead and  provide the audience with some closing  remarks before we close today just to  say thank you to everybody for listening  to this short presentation I appreciate  it I hope you found it valuable thank  you and before I go I want to thank Rob  roots and our sponsor recommend Coulter  for making today's educational webcast  possible I'd also like to remind  audience members that today's webcast  will be available for on-demand viewing  at this month you will receive an email  from lab roots letting you know when the  webcast will be available for replay  please share that announcement with your  colleagues whom you miss today's live  event that's all for now and thanks for  joining us we hope to see you again soon  bye bye thank you thank you bye bye
 

